  "summary_en": "Law Commission project page summarising its February 2023 advice to the UK Government on remote driving beyond line-of-sight on public roads. It finds the current law a grey area and recommends a statutory licensing scheme, a ban on remote driving from abroad, no-fault compensation, and short-term amendments to construction and use regulations.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Remote driving is legally a grey area: neither prohibited nor expressly allowed.",
   "Propose a statutory licensing scheme, including an Entity for Remote Driving Operation (ERDO) licence.",
   "Ban remote driving from abroad until international agreements are in place.",
   "No-fault compensation for victims of collisions involving remote drivers.",
   "Short term: amend Construction and Use Regulations 1986; require a safety driver unless a Vehicle Special Order applies."
